      "publisher": "X1 Wind",
      "title": "X1 Wind Closes Strategic Funding to Accelerate Floating Wind",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.x1wind.com/news/x1-wind-closes-strategic-funding-to-accelerate-floating-wind/",
      "publishedDate": "2026-09-09",
      "retrievedAt": "2026-10-05T12:00:00Z",
      "collectionMethod": "manual",
      "sourceText": "X1 Wind announced closing its fourth strategic funding round, led by Grow Ventures with Avancsa acquiring a similar share and existing investors converting prior instruments. The funding supports X1 Wind's transition from technology validation toward commercial deployment, including the NextFloat X100 8.5 MW platform at the PlemCat test site, with manufacturing expected in 2027.",
      "licenseNote": "Public company webpage; reuse terms not yet reviewed."
    },
    {
      "sourceRecordId": "eng-src-2026-09-20-ore-catapult-celtic-sea-mammals",
      "candidateStatus": "candidate",
      "sourceType": "trade_association",
      "publisher": "Offshore Renewable Energy Catapult",
      "title": "New smart tech to capture large scale marine mammal behaviour in the Celtic Sea",
      "sourceUrl": "https://ore.catapult.org.uk/media-centre/press-releases/new-smart-tech-to-capture-large-scale-marine-mammal-behaviour-in-the-celtic-sea",
      "publishedDate": "2026-09-15",
      "retrievedAt": "2026-10-05T12:00:00Z",
      "collectionMethod": "manual",
      "sourceText": "ORE Catapult launched the GBP 2.7 million SubSea Soundscape project with Celtic Sea Power and the University of Exeter, funded by The Crown Estate's OWEC programme. The three-year project uses 21 seabed-mounted acoustic recorders across the Celtic Sea to establish marine mammal and underwater-noise evidence for floating offshore wind planning and consenting.",
      "licenseNote": "Public research-institution webpage; reuse terms not yet reviewed."
    }
  ],
